  data: {
    LLM: "1. Each player turns over their top card simultaneously. 2. The highest card wins all cards in the trick. 3. Winning cards are placed at the bottom of the winner's deck. 4. Exception: An Ace is the highest card, UNLESS a 6 is played against it. A 6 beats an Ace (but loses to every other card).",
    Player: "1. Each player turns over their top card simultaneously. 2. The highest card wins all cards in the trick. 3. Winning cards are placed at the bottom of the winner's deck. 4. Exception: An Ace is the highest card, UNLESS a 6 is played against it. A 6 beats an Ace (but loses to every other card).",
    objective: 'Capture the entire deck by winning tricks: each round players reveal the top card simultaneously; the higher rank takes the trick (six beats ace). The player who collects all the cards wins; the opponent left with no cards is the loser, the drunkard.',
